# docs-site (documentation only)

This Next.js app is **not** the Occasio product. Do not add creator, vault, or billing flows here.

## Allowed

- Edit `docs-site/content/*.md` (PRD, TRD, blueprint, wireframes)
- Update `docs-site/src/lib/navigation.ts` when adding doc pages
- Mermaid in markdown (` ```mermaid ` blocks)
- Future: marketing landing + optional public `/c/[slug]` recipient page

## Not allowed

- Duplicating mobile screens as the main product UI
- Firebase/auth logic for the creator app
- New product features that belong in `src/features/`

## Adding a doc page

1. Create `docs-site/content/<slug>.md` with frontmatter (`title`, `description`, `phase`, `updated`)
2. Register in `docs-site/src/lib/navigation.ts`
3. Update `docs-site/content/blueprint.md` if phase status changes

## Source of truth for product code

Mobile: `src/` + `ARCHITECTURE.md` + `AGENTS.md`

Legacy `docs/prd-trd.md` — prefer split `content/prd.md` + `content/trd.md`.
